.TH TIMERC-BG 1 "2026" "timerc 1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
timerc-bg \- start a timerc timer in the background
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B timerc-bg
[\fItime\fR] [\fItask\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B timerc-bg
is the same program as
.BR timerc (1),
selected by the name it is run under. It accepts exactly the same time formats,
switches and options, but detaches from the terminal (double fork, new session,
stdio to /dev/null) and returns to the shell immediately. The timer keeps
running after the terminal or SSH session is closed.
.PP
Use
.B timerc
instead when a script should wait for the timer to finish.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
timerc-bg 25m focus
timerc-bg d1h        # shut down in one hour
.fi
.SH FILES
Same as
.BR timerc (1);
errors are written to \fI~/.config/timerc/timer.log\fR since there is no terminal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR timerc (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mohamad Almousli <https://al-mo.de>
